{"id":"4a1f43a4ba47d054","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-category-baire.md","title":"Baire Category Theorem","display":"thm-category-baire — Baire Category Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-category-baire","aliases":["58-thm-category-baire"],"display":"thm-category-baire — Baire Category Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-category-baire"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-category-baire</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-category-baire — Baire Category Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"05d80cd20b53d8a2\" href=\"?note=05d80cd20b53d8a2\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md\">../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,d,U\\in V\">\\(X,d,U\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\">\\(\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\\)</span> is the complete-metric-space predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"05d80cd20b53d8a2\" href=\"?note=05d80cd20b53d8a2\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md\">../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))\\)</span> types a sequence of subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}category-baire}\\vdash{}\n&amp;\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\\land X\\neq\\emptyset\n\\to \\forall U\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\Bigl[\n\\bigl(\\forall x\\in U(n)\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U(n))\\bigr)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\exists y\\in U(n)\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to \\exists x\\in X\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x\\in U(n))\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}category-baire}\\vdash{}\n&amp;\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\\land X\\neq\\emptyset\n\\to \\forall U\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\Bigl[\n\\bigl(\\forall x\\in U(n)\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U(n))\\bigr)\\land\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\bigl(\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\exists y\\in U(n)\\;(d(x,y)&lt;\\varepsilon)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to \\exists x\\in X\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x\\in U(n))\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The two expanded clauses say respectively that every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U(n)\">\\(U(n)\\)</span> is open and dense in the topology induced by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>; this avoids an undeclared <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DenseOpen}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DenseOpen}_S\\)</span> predicate.</li>\n<li>The nonemptiness assumption is necessary for the displayed common-point consequence; the empty metric space is complete.</li>\n<li>It is fundamental in analysis and functional analysis.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md","status":"resolved","id":"05d80cd20b53d8a2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md","status":"resolved","id":"05d80cd20b53d8a2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)$ is the complete-metric-space predicate from [[../batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,d,U\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}category-baire}\\vdash{}\n&\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\\land X\\neq\\emptyset\n\\to \\forall U\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(U,\\omega,\\mathcal P(X))\\land\\\\\n&\\quad\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\Bigl[\n\\bigl(\\forall x\\in U(n)\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\forall y\\in X\\;(d(x,y)<\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U(n))\\bigr)\\land\\\\\n&\\qquad\\bigl(\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\n\\exists y\\in U(n)\\;(d(x,y)<\\varepsilon)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr]\\\\\n&\\quad\\to \\exists x\\in X\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(x\\in U(n))\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"U(n)","display":false},{"tex":"d","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DenseOpen}_S","display":false}],"bytes":1514,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4069","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-thm-category-baire.md|58-thm-category-baire]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["05d80cd20b53d8a2","36d7463d215be751"]}